course: dictionary
lesson: 1713
title: The body clock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Circadian is a long word, but the text around it gives you the meaning. «The body clock, or circadian rhythm, runs on about 24 hours, matching one spin of the Earth.» The words "or" and "body clock" tell you that circadian rhythm is another name for the body clock.
explain: The second example gives a clue too: «Your body has its own clock, called the body clock or circadian rhythm ("about a day"), which runs on about 24 hours.» The words "about a day" show that circadian is about a day long.
explain: Now test your idea by swapping it into a sentence: «My circadian clock tells me it is time to sleep.» It still makes sense, so circadian must mean to do with the body's daily clock.
fact: Circadian means to do with the body's natural daily clock.
fact: A circadian rhythm is a cycle of about 24 hours.
fact: «Circadian» comes from Latin words meaning "about a day".
fact: Your circadian rhythm helps control when you sleep, wake up and feel hungry.
fact: Plants and animals have circadian rhythms too.
exercise: «The body clock, or circadian rhythm, runs on about 24 hours.» What does circadian mean? | A type of very fast running | To do with the weather in summer | *To do with the body's natural daily clock | To do with the bones in your legs
exercise: Ella feels sleepy at night and wide awake in the morning. Which science idea explains this? | Jet lag from a long flight | *Circadian rhythm | A sudden drop in temperature | A broken bone
exercise: What length of time does a circadian rhythm cycle last? | A month | *About 24 hours | A week | An hour
test: Why can screens before bed keep you awake? | Because they make your body clock disappear | Because they make you hungry all night | *Because they can disturb your circadian rhythm | Because they make you too hot
test: Which phrase means the same as circadian rhythm? | Pulse | *Body clock | Heart rate | Digestion
exam: Jet lag happens when your circadian clock is out of step with a new time zone. What does circadian most nearly mean? | Fast and furious | Very cold | *Daily body clock | Shiny and bright
